<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple Computer//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  THIS UNIT LIVES IN /Library/LaunchDaemons, NOT /System/Library/LaunchDaemons,
  AND THAT IS LOAD-BEARING.

  launchd's embedded bootstrap on this firmware carries
  `Bootstrap > Paths = [/System/Library/LaunchDaemons]` -- one directory, and
  it really is the only one walked at boot. /Library/LaunchDaemons does not
  exist on stock and launchd never scans it. That sounds like an argument for
  putting this unit in the system directory, and it is exactly backwards.

  The binary this unit runs is ours, which means it is ad-hoc signed by us,
  which means AMFI rejects it on a clean boot. A unit in
  /System/Library/LaunchDaemons would be loaded at the one moment its program
  cannot possibly execute. This project already learned that the expensive
  way: docs/HISTORY.md's "sshd never started because launchd does not scan
  /Library/LaunchDaemons" entry records a loader unit that was impossible
  exactly when it was needed and redundant exactly when it was possible, and
  it was deleted outright.

  What actually loads this directory is the untether itself. After
  etasonuntether's payload takes tfp0 and patches AMFI/sandbox/cs_enforcement,
  it runs its own `launchctl load /Library/LaunchDaemons` one-liner. So a unit
  here is loaded AFTER the kernel has been patched -- which is the only point
  in the boot where an unsigned third-party binary can run at all. sshd comes
  up by precisely this path today.

  The consequence to be aware of: on a device where the untether has not run
  (a tethered boot off our own patched kernel, or a device whose persistence
  is broken), this never fires. That is correct rather than unfortunate --
  there is no trust store to fix if the jailbreak is not running.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
      <string>xyz.regulad.blackb0x.cainjector</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
      <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/usr/share/blackb0x/cainjector/run.sh</string>
      </array>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
      <string>/usr/share/blackb0x/cainjector/cainjector.err.log</string>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
      <string>/usr/share/blackb0x/cainjector/cainjector.out.log</string>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
      <true/>
    <key>UserName</key>
      <string>root</string>
</dict>
</plist>
